Defend an advanced mine plan under geological and operating uncertainty (@mine-planning-project: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mining-and-mineral-engineering, #source "../sources/Operations-Research-in-Mine-Planning.lingua#r_3WX1KW34EWEGYZ6HGEMGGQBKHS", #source "../sources/MineLib-Benchmarks-and-Methods.lingua#r_3KXVJNVZ2FSQ8CZJMJG2JDQYR8", #source "../sources/Resource-and-Reserve-Reporting-CRIRSCO-CBRR.lingua#r_2CZZ64T1W8VC542VCNCH2E6DSR", #source "../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA", #mining-and-mineral-engineering "Advanced-ground-model-design-and-observational-study.lingua#r_7WBJ5RG8F7YE3J2DP6KK1KCFTQ") { r_5Y2NXQ412NVQNSD0MDVHBWQW4K
**Read:** [A Review of Operations Research in Mine Planning — Newman and colleagues](../sources/Operations-Research-in-Mine-Planning.lingua#r_3WX1KW34EWEGYZ6HGEMGGQBKHS), the entire review and full primary method papers selected from it; [MineLib — Espinoza, Goycoolea, Moreno, and Newman](../sources/MineLib-Benchmarks-and-Methods.lingua#r_3KXVJNVZ2FSQ8CZJMJG2JDQYR8), the complete paper/formulations and the exact chosen benchmark definitions; [Resources, reserves, and technical-study definitions — CRIRSCO and CBRR](../sources/Resource-and-Reserve-Reporting-CRIRSCO-CBRR.lingua#r_2CZZ64T1W8VC542VCNCH2E6DSR), the complete relevant technical-study and resource/reserve definitions; [Hard Rock Miner’s Handbook — Jack de la Vergne, fifth edition](../sources/Hard-Rock-Miners-Handbook.lingua#r_18YBY5XX4TFS7ZQSKTQMW34EFA), all sections needed for the full layout/equipment/system comparison.

Use an authorized public benchmark or documented deposit case and preserve the source, licence, geological domain, block support, coordinate frame, and parameter meaning. Read the complete Newman review and MineLib paper/formulation, then the full primary method papers actually implemented. A benchmark's preprocessed blocks and precedences do not supply missing geological, geotechnical, community, or permitting evidence.

Define the method, layout/access, extraction dependencies, material destinations, dilution/loss assumptions, processing response, capacities, time, inventory, and objective. Derive the model and independently verify feasibility, balance closure, and reported value. Reproduce the small original exhaustive example before relying on a large solver; independently test at least one reduced instance and document optimality bounds/gaps.

Compare a deterministic plan with geological/processing scenarios and at least one alternative sequencing or adaptive formulation. Separate expected value, variability, adverse outcomes, and the decisions actually available before new information arrives. Avoid granting perfect future knowledge to a supposedly practical adaptive plan.

**Work:** deliver a defended planning study with an independently checkable baseline, two materially different designs, a defined operating transition, sensitivity/uncertainty, and a credible observation/update strategy. Compare with published benchmark or case results on identical assumptions before interpreting differences. State which unmodeled ground, ventilation, water, access, work, and closure constraints could change feasibility or ranking. A mathematical optimum is one piece of a mine design, not its final proof.

**Continue:** [Compare ground mechanisms and design predictions against independent observations](Advanced-ground-model-design-and-observational-study.lingua#r_7WBJ5RG8F7YE3J2DP6KK1KCFTQ).

**Return:** [Mining and mineral engineering — extraction, processing, and continuing work](../Mining-and-mineral-engineering.lingua#r_22HJPS3RTK5EX1J55YJP75PHYA).
